cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "bem-fem-fsi: a free-wake panel method coupled to a three-dimensional finite element solid"
abstract: >-
  A Python code computing the unsteady loads on a deformable finite wing in
  incompressible flow and the deformation those loads produce. The fluid is a
  free-wake source-doublet panel method that sheds one wake strip per time step
  and convects it as material fluid, so the added mass is predicted by the
  unsteady Bernoulli relation rather than modelled. The structure is a
  three-dimensional finite element solid of eight-node hexahedra with
  incompatible modes, in which stress and tangent modulus are evaluated at each
  Gauss point by a material object, so anisotropic and inelastic materials
  extend the code rather than rewrite it; isotropic elasticity, orthotropic
  elasticity and Kelvin-Voigt viscoelasticity are provided. The two solvers are
  coupled by a partitioned scheme whose interface conserves force, moment and
  virtual work to round-off and reproduces rigid-body motion exactly,
  accelerated by Aitken relaxation or IQN-ILS, strongly enough for water, where
  the added mass exceeds the structural mass and a staggered scheme has no
  stable step size. The panel method is carried in verbatim from its own
  repository and is not modified here.
type: software
